    "strategy": "Fresh Actestra profile v1; native AionUi profiles remain untouched. Forward-only schema v7 retains schemas v1-v6 exactly, adds a revisioned General Work recovery journal, and keeps all Actestra SQLite ownership—including existing AionUI shadow evidence, approval authority, workspace grants, bounded content references, terminal evidence, and recovery checkpoints—behind one supervised Electron persistence utility protocol. AgentAdapter v2 runs each General Worker attempt in one separately supervised Electron utility process with exact main-owned identities and events. The scoped main-process gateway remains limited to bounded workspace UTF-8 read and create-only task-output UTF-8 write. GW-P4.5 now persists tool ambiguity, artifact ownership, event order, terminal cleanup, and Task/Session/Worker reconciliation before acknowledging or releasing an attempt, and performs deterministic startup recovery before the preserved AionUI window is created. No renderer, route, Goose, CrewAI, shell, arbitrary network, credential, MCP, or second state authority is added.",
    "rollback": "Regenerate without patch 0009 to remove AionUI startup recovery wiring while retaining GW-P4.4 scoped native tools and the General Worker. Regenerate without patch 0008 to remove the scoped native tool platform while retaining GW-P4.3. Regenerate without patch 0007 to remove the General Worker process probe and Adapter v2 entry while retaining the persistence utility. Existing schema v7 checkpoints and schema v6 rows remain inert and are never rewritten or deleted; use a fresh Actestra profile for a true data downgrade. The frozen AionUi foundation and native AionUi profiles stay byte-identical."
  },
